Yolov8s, designed for efficient identification of micro-objects [14], features
a foundational network balancing speed and accuracy. With a streamlined
design, the model was trained using a batch size of 16 over 100 epochs and
a learning rate of 0.01. The dataset, totalling 500 images, was thoughtfully
divided, allocating 75% for training, 20% for validation, and the rest for
testing. Remarkably, the entire 100 epochs completed in just 0.647 hours,
emphasizing the swift convergence and robust computational capabilities of
the Yolov8s architecture.
